{"_section": "3 — Fault-injection scenario comment (HDC8 property 6)", "_note": "Fault-injection of timeout, inactivity, and focus loss produces no SignoffAct record and no release-class action. This is a behavioural invariant enforced at runtime; the schema demonstrates it structurally: a release-class action (order, prescription, referral, patient-visible diagnostic statement per MAK-FFC PF-8) requires exactly one committed SignoffAct with fabric_entry. No timeout event, inactivity period, or focus-loss event may produce a SignoffAct. The absence of any SignoffAct in the encounter's fabric entries = no release pathway exists. Test: inject each fault class; assert encounter fabric entries contain zero SignoffAct records; assert zero release-class downstream events emitted."}
